<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.12.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01458</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.12.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>b5b68d93-66db-4111-9d4a-8e1e11a5ea07</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para><emphasis><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></emphasis></para>
<para>
  For questions 1 - 5, use the the three exponential functions defined below:
</para>

<list>
  <item>\(f(x)=100 \cdot 3^x\)</item>
  <item>\(g(x)=100 \cdot (3.5)^x\)</item>
  <item>\(h(x)=100 \cdot 4^x\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> Which of these functions grows the least quickly?  </item>
</list>
<para> <emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(f(x)\) </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item> Which function grows the most quickly? </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para> <emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(h(x)\) </para>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
    <item> The three given graphs represent \(f\), \(g\), and \(h\). Which graph corresponds to each function? </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/2444927a1ca141b0eb7e8e4cb8a5535e3d515ca9"/></media></figure></para>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">

    <item>Which graph corresponds to \(f(x)\)?</item>

  </list>
</list>
<para> <emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(f(x)\) </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">

    <item>Which graph corresponds to \(g(x)\)?</item>
  </list>
</list>
<para> <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Graph B </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">

    <item>Which graph corresponds to \(h(x)\)?</item>
  </list>
</list>
<para> <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Graph A </para>

<para>For questions 6 - 8, use the given graphs of three exponential equations. 
</para>

<para><figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/0f2d9390501d73022c2c55459c70ba69b67dceea"/></media></figure></para>
<para>Match each equation with its graph.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(y=20 \cdot 3^x\)</item>
</list>
<para> <emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>Graph M </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(y=50 \cdot 3^x\)</item>
</list>
<para> <emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>Graph L </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(y=100 \cdot 3^x\)</item>
</list>
<para> <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Graph K </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">
  <para>For questions 9 - 10, use the graph below. </para>

</list>
<para><figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/ae45c15b137051cffebf78e6eebe59553caa0d11"/></media></figure></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">

    <item> Written in the form \(f(x)=a \cdot b^x\), what is the value of \(a\)<emphasis> </emphasis>for each function? Do not enter commas or spaces in your answer. </item>
</list>
<para> <emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>160 </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="10" type="enumerated">
    <item> Which graph decreases the most quickly? </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para> <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Graph C </para>

  <para>The graphs of \(y=50 \cdot 2^x\), \(y=200 \cdot 2^x\), and \(y=100 \cdot 2^x\) are shown.</para>
  
    
    <figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/e96bced7e4da7adf86f2dfe1ea3f8c4d446e192e"/></media></figure><list class="os-raise-noindent" start="11" type="enumerated">

    <item>Which is the graph of \(y=100 \cdot 2^x\)?
  </item>
</list>
<para> <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Graph B </para>
<para>For questions 12 – 14, use the graph below:</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Graph of six exponential functions."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/a3588f5079a44777c05412324d2a3176b0b499d5"/></media></figure></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="12" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which of the functions graphed, \(y=a \cdot b^x\), has the smallest value for \(a\)?</item>
</list>
<para> <emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>F </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="13" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which of the functions graphed, \(y=a \cdot b^x\), has the lowest value for \(b\)?</item>
</list>
<para> <emphasis>Answer</emphasis><emphasis>: </emphasis>C </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="14" type="enumerated">
  <item>What is the equation of the horizontal asymptote for \(f(x)=5 \cdot 2^x-3\)?  </item></list>

    <list>
      <item> \(y=2\) </item>
      <item> \(y=3\) </item>
      <item> \(y=-3\) </item>
      <item> \(y=5\) </item>
    </list>

<para> <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> c. \(y=-3\) </para></section>
</content>
